+       identity, hard-feasibility preservation, deterministic tie breaks,
+       abstention, cost accounting, circular verdict class, and bare fields.
+    2. Recompute every held-out headroom group from raw certification rows.
+       Exclude groups without both a correct and incorrect candidate from the
+       primary selection effect, but report them as opportunity rows.
+    3. Freeze four selectors before scoring: model likelihood; exact feasibility
+       with likelihood tie-break; certified PWA residual without exact filtering;
+       and exact hard feasibility followed by PWA residual. Use one stable final
+       tie-break and a fixed abstention threshold learned on calibration only.
